afc93e57 (850 1793305329752 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f385") (src . "publish-landing names a library with no path by its id, apart from paths\n\nfile-scope-changes labelled a holder with no path field \"(no path) <id>\",\na string that a real stored path can equal: a library stored at that\npath and the pathless library it spells were then named as one entry,\nand the second change was not named at all. A pathless holder is now\nlabelled by the list (no-path <id>), never by a string, and the answer\nis the changed paths sorted, then one (no-path <id>) per changed\npathless holder, sorted by id. Without a filter only holders with a\npath are compared, so landing-freeze and landing-commit still get\nstrings only. publish-landing's datum-not-published refusal carries\n(paths ...) always, empty when only pathless libraries changed, and\n(no-path <id> ...) only when one did. A library whose path is removed\nbetween the cuts is named in both: its old path and its id.\n\n- landing-files.sc: the label, an equal? table, the answer's order.\n- tools/publish-landing.sc: the refusal's two clauses.\n- README: the publisher section.\n- Tests: publish-landing (a library stored at the path \"(no path) <id>\"\n  beside library <id> with no path; two pathless libraries in id order;\n  no no-path clause on a paths-only refusal; the unfiltered comparison\n  still answers strings only); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 523))))
